-- IL-ONE-MEANING-1 (2026-10-26, charter pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000437, 1000455, 1000438, 1000445, 1000444, 1000454, 1000453 and the chaos drill 1000422; owner directive of 2026-10-26 08:30Z "one meaning per breach", BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1)
--
-- WHAT WAS MEASURED (qnfo-audit SELECT only, 2026-10-26 17:55-20:20Z)
--   BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1 (migrations/2026-10-26-breach-one-meaning.sql) disabled the triggers of six metrics because each repeats the meaning of another metric that keeps its trigger:
--   fleet_ai_run_rate_30d_usd (409), workers_ai_run_rate_usd (3687) and fleet_cost_run_rate_usd (3688) sit inside monthly_cost_run_rate_usd (trigger 3689, open critical issue 99938);
--   open_issues_without_doer_120m (5944) and issues_without_next_action (1959) are the issue-with-no-doer meaning that issues_over_24h_no_doer (trigger 9901) keeps; issue_mttr_h_30d (410) is mttr_h_7d (3464).
--   IMPROVEMENT-LOOP-1 (qnfo-fleet-control improvementEvaluate) does not read the triggers' enabled flag: a metric whose triggers are all disabled keeps its trend and relapse checks on purpose (its test pins that), and
--   only an explicit "[superseded by <metric>" marker in metric_registry.target retires the check (IL-SUPERSEDED-1, 0.34.0; SLA-120M-2 and SLA-120M-6 used it). The six metrics carry no marker, so the loop filed a second ticket
--   for each meaning: 12 open METRIC-REGRESSION-1 and METRIC-FIX-RELAPSED-1 issues on 2026-10-26 20:20Z (1000437, 1000455, 1000438, 1000466, 1000445, 1000485, 1000444, 1000454, 1000453, 1000504, 1000468, and 1000467 for papers_live_failing_release_gate).
--   The cost trio reads the Oct 19-21 research burst through a trailing 7-day mean compared with the prior 7 days (7d mean 866.97 against 222.63 for fleet_ai_run_rate_30d_usd), so the regression cannot clear for about two weeks even
--   though cost_daily workers_ai fell from 55.31 USD on 2026-10-19 to 10.19 on 2026-10-26; the cost breach itself is carried by monthly_cost_run_rate_usd (1466.84 against a trigger of 650) and by issue 99938.
--   The chaos drill control improvement-loop-superseded-marker (control_alternate_probes, issue 1000422) checks that the successors named in the control (issues_open_over_120m and open_issues_without_doer_120m) carry an enabled
--   trigger; trigger 5944 was disabled by BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1, so the drill read the alternate as broken (last_pass 0 at 13:01Z: a successor metric of a superseded one has no enabled trigger). The drill is right about the
--   state and wrong about the design: the successor of open_issues_without_doer_120m is now issues_over_24h_no_doer.
--
-- WHAT THIS FILE CHANGES (data only: no worker, trigger or cron)
--   1. The six metrics get the marker " [superseded by <successor>, IL-ONE-MEANING-1]" appended to metric_registry.target, only while the successor has an enabled trigger. Every metric stays measured and keeps its history;
--      thresholds, caps and triggers are not touched. The loop closes the open tickets itself with the superseded-by evidence (IL-SUPERSEDED-1), and each ticket also gets a measuring contract (item 4).
--      The three owner-outcome metrics (subscribers_growth_monthly, outreach_reply_rate_30d, social_engagement_rate_30d: triggers disabled on purpose 2026-10-18, REDERIVE-2026-10-18 OWNER-OUTCOME) get the marker
--      " [owner-outcome: not autonomically closable, IL-OWNER-OUTCOME-1]" that the code task IL-OWNER-OUTCOME-1 teaches the loop to read; it changes nothing until that task lands.
--   2. The drill probe of control improvement-loop-superseded-marker follows the chain: every marker names a registered successor that carries an enabled trigger or is itself superseded. The control's alternate text and
--      evidence say so. It still fails when a successor is missing or its trigger is disabled and no marker continues the chain.
--   3. The failure mode il-duplicate-meaning with a detector: an open METRIC-REGRESSION-1 or METRIC-FIX-RELAPSED-1 ticket on a metric whose triggers BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1 disabled and that carries no marker. It reads 11 before
--      and 0 after (papers_live_failing_release_gate is excluded: its trigger was disabled because it contradicts an owner directive and it has no successor metric; the loop files it as an early warning only).
--   4. A contract on class issue-<id> for each open ticket of the six metrics (module il-one-meaning-1): carried = the marker is in place and the successor has an enabled trigger. Issue 1000422 gets the drill probe as its contract.
--   5. Two issues with a doer for the two loop defects this file does not fix in data: IL-OWNER-OUTCOME-1 and IL-TRIGGER-AWARE-1 (code tasks for the code loop on qnfo-fleet-control/worker.js, which another claim holds).
-- Not touched: the tickets of the owner-outcome metrics and the regressions of metrics whose trigger is clear (IL-OWNER-OUTCOME-1 and IL-TRIGGER-AWARE-1 carry them).
-- The old texts are in bak_20261026_il_one_meaning first. The Rollback line reads it only for the control's long alternate text: it removes the markers, restores the old probe, and returns the contracts to monitoring.
-- Every UPDATE is anchored on the text it changes or on a marker, so a second apply, or a text someone has since changed, is left alone.
--
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- BACKUP: bak_20261026_il_one_meaning
-- Rollback: UPDATE metric_registry SET target = replace(replace(replace(replace(target, ' [superseded by monthly_cost_run_rate_usd, IL-ONE-MEANING-1]', ''), ' [superseded by issues_over_24h_no_doer, IL-ONE-MEANING-1]', ''), ' [superseded by mttr_h_7d, IL-ONE-MEANING-1]', ''), ' [owner-outcome: not autonomically closable, IL-OWNER-OUTCOME-1]', '') WHERE instr(target, 'IL-ONE-MEANING-1') > 0 OR instr(target, 'IL-OWNER-OUTCOME-1') > 0; UPDATE control_alternate_probes SET probe_sql = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM analytics_metric_triggers WHERE metric_key IN (''issues_open_over_120m'', ''open_issues_without_doer_120m'') AND enabled = 1) < 2 THEN ''a successor metric of a superseded one has no enabled trigger'' WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM metric_registry WHERE metric IN (''issues_open_over_120m'', ''open_issues_without_doer_120m'')) < 2 THEN ''a successor metric is not in metric_registry'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed', window_note = replace(window_note, ' | IL-ONE-MEANING-1 2026-10-26: every superseded marker in metric_registry names a successor that is registered and either carries an enabled trigger or is itself superseded, so the chain ends in a metric with a trigger (issues_open_over_120m, issues_over_24h_no_doer, monthly_cost_run_rate_usd, mttr_h_7d on 2026-10-26). It replaces the check of the two named successors because BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1 disabled trigger 5944 of open_issues_without_doer_120m as a duplicate of issues_over_24h_no_doer, which is the condition the old probe read as a failed alternate (agent_issues 1000422).', '') WHERE control = 'improvement-loop-superseded-marker' AND instr(probe_sql, 'no metric carries a superseded marker') > 0; UPDATE control_registry SET alternate_path = (SELECT old_text FROM bak_20261026_il_one_meaning WHERE src = 'control_registry.alternate_path'), evidence = replace(evidence, ' | IL-ONE-MEANING-1 2026-10-26: BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1 disabled the triggers of six metrics as duplicates of one successor each, so IMPROVEMENT-LOOP-1 kept filing a second ticket for the same meaning (METRIC-REGRESSION-1 and METRIC-FIX-RELAPSED-1: 12 open on 2026-10-26 20:20Z); each of the six now carries this marker with its successor, and the drill probe follows the chain to a metric with an enabled trigger. The alternate was exercised by the 13:01Z drill, which read the disabled trigger 5944 and failed (agent_issues 1000422).', '') WHERE control = 'improvement-loop-superseded-marker' AND instr(alternate_path, 'issues_over_24h_no_doer') > 0; UPDATE remediation_contracts SET status = 'monitoring', last_verdict = NULL, next_due_at = datetime('now') WHERE module = 'il-one-meaning-1'; DELETE FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = 'fm-il-duplicate-meaning'; DELETE FROM failure_modes WHERE fm_key = 'il-duplicate-meaning'
-- Rollback note: decision_log stays (append-only); the two filed issues stay open until a code-probe or a closing record resolves them.

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261026_il_one_meaning AS
  SELECT 'metric_registry.target' AS src, metric AS name, target AS old_text FROM metric_registry WHERE metric IN ('fleet_ai_run_rate_30d_usd', 'workers_ai_run_rate_usd', 'fleet_cost_run_rate_usd', 'open_issues_without_doer_120m', 'issues_without_next_action', 'issue_mttr_h_30d', 'subscribers_growth_monthly', 'outreach_reply_rate_30d', 'social_engagement_rate_30d')
  UNION ALL SELECT 'control_alternate_probes.probe_sql', control, probe_sql FROM control_alternate_probes WHERE control = 'improvement-loop-superseded-marker'
  UNION ALL SELECT 'control_alternate_probes.window_note', control, window_note FROM control_alternate_probes WHERE control = 'improvement-loop-superseded-marker';
INSERT INTO bak_20261026_il_one_meaning (src, name, old_text)
  SELECT 'control_registry.alternate_path', control, alternate_path FROM control_registry WHERE control = 'improvement-loop-superseded-marker' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM bak_20261026_il_one_meaning WHERE src = 'control_registry.alternate_path')
  UNION ALL SELECT 'control_registry.evidence', control, evidence FROM control_registry WHERE control = 'improvement-loop-superseded-marker' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM bak_20261026_il_one_meaning WHERE src = 'control_registry.evidence');
INSERT INTO bak_20261026_il_one_meaning (src, name, old_text)
  SELECT 'remediation_contracts', class, verify_probe || char(10) || action || char(10) || status || char(10) || COALESCE(module, '') FROM remediation_contracts
  WHERE class IN (SELECT 'issue-' || id FROM agent_issues WHERE status = 'open' AND (title LIKE 'METRIC-REGRESSION-1: %' OR title LIKE 'METRIC-FIX-RELAPSED-1: %' OR id = 1000422))
    AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM bak_20261026_il_one_meaning b WHERE b.src = 'remediation_contracts' AND b.name = remediation_contracts.class);

-- 1. The markers (only while the successor has an enabled trigger).
UPDATE metric_registry SET target = target || ' [superseded by monthly_cost_run_rate_usd, IL-ONE-MEANING-1]'
WHERE metric IN ('fleet_ai_run_rate_30d_usd', 'workers_ai_run_rate_usd', 'fleet_cost_run_rate_usd') AND instr(COALESCE(target, ''), '[superseded by') = 0
  AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM analytics_metric_triggers WHERE metric_key = 'monthly_cost_run_rate_usd' AND enabled = 1);

UPDATE metric_registry SET target = target || ' [superseded by issues_over_24h_no_doer, IL-ONE-MEANING-1]'
WHERE metric IN ('open_issues_without_doer_120m', 'issues_without_next_action') AND instr(COALESCE(target, ''), '[superseded by') = 0
  AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM analytics_metric_triggers WHERE metric_key = 'issues_over_24h_no_doer' AND enabled = 1);

UPDATE metric_registry SET target = target || ' [superseded by mttr_h_7d, IL-ONE-MEANING-1]'
WHERE metric IN ('issue_mttr_h_30d') AND instr(COALESCE(target, ''), '[superseded by') = 0
  AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM analytics_metric_triggers WHERE metric_key = 'mttr_h_7d' AND enabled = 1);

UPDATE metric_registry SET target = target || ' [owner-outcome: not autonomically closable, IL-OWNER-OUTCOME-1]'
WHERE metric IN ('subscribers_growth_monthly', 'outreach_reply_rate_30d', 'social_engagement_rate_30d') AND instr(COALESCE(target, ''), '[owner-outcome') = 0
  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM analytics_metric_triggers t WHERE t.metric_key = metric_registry.metric AND t.enabled = 1);

-- 2. The drill probe follows the chain; the control's text and evidence say so.
UPDATE control_alternate_probes SET probe_sql = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM metric_registry WHERE instr(COALESCE(target, ''''), ''[superseded by '') > 0) THEN ''no metric carries a superseded marker, so the control filters nothing'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM metric_registry r WHERE instr(COALESCE(r.target, ''''), ''[superseded by '') > 0 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM metric_registry s WHERE instr(r.target, ''[superseded by '' || s.metric || '','') > 0 OR instr(r.target, ''[superseded by '' || s.metric || '']'') > 0 OR instr(r.target, ''[superseded by '' || s.metric || '' '') > 0)) THEN ''a successor metric is not in metric_registry'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM metric_registry r WHERE instr(COALESCE(r.target, ''''), ''[superseded by '') > 0 AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM metric_registry s WHERE (instr(r.target, ''[superseded by '' || s.metric || '','') > 0 OR instr(r.target, ''[superseded by '' || s.metric || '']'') > 0 OR instr(r.target, ''[superseded by '' || s.metric || '' '') > 0) AND (instr(COALESCE(s.target, ''''), ''[superseded by '') > 0 OR EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM analytics_metric_triggers t WHERE t.metric_key = s.metric AND t.enabled = 1)))) THEN ''a successor metric of a superseded one has no enabled trigger'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  window_note = window_note || ' | IL-ONE-MEANING-1 2026-10-26: every superseded marker in metric_registry names a successor that is registered and either carries an enabled trigger or is itself superseded, so the chain ends in a metric with a trigger (issues_open_over_120m, issues_over_24h_no_doer, monthly_cost_run_rate_usd, mttr_h_7d on 2026-10-26). It replaces the check of the two named successors because BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1 disabled trigger 5944 of open_issues_without_doer_120m as a duplicate of issues_over_24h_no_doer, which is the condition the old probe read as a failed alternate (agent_issues 1000422).'
WHERE control = 'improvement-loop-superseded-marker' AND instr(probe_sql, 'no metric carries a superseded marker') = 0 AND instr(probe_sql, 'open_issues_without_doer_120m') > 0;

UPDATE control_registry SET alternate_path = 'the successor metric carries its own enabled trigger (issues_open_over_120m trigger 5937; issues_over_24h_no_doer trigger 9901 for the no-doer meaning of open_issues_without_doer_120m and issues_without_next_action; monthly_cost_run_rate_usd trigger 3689 for the three partial cost run rates fleet_ai_run_rate_30d_usd, workers_ai_run_rate_usd and fleet_cost_run_rate_usd; mttr_h_7d trigger 3464 for issue_mttr_h_30d) and is still judged by the loop; the superseded metric stays measured in metric_history. Only the explicit marker disqualifies: other registry metrics whose triggers are disabled for other reasons keep their regression and relapse checks.',
  evidence = evidence || ' | IL-ONE-MEANING-1 2026-10-26: BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1 disabled the triggers of six metrics as duplicates of one successor each, so IMPROVEMENT-LOOP-1 kept filing a second ticket for the same meaning (METRIC-REGRESSION-1 and METRIC-FIX-RELAPSED-1: 12 open on 2026-10-26 20:20Z); each of the six now carries this marker with its successor, and the drill probe follows the chain to a metric with an enabled trigger. The alternate was exercised by the 13:01Z drill, which read the disabled trigger 5944 and failed (agent_issues 1000422).', reviewed_at = strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')
WHERE control = 'improvement-loop-superseded-marker' AND instr(alternate_path, 'issues_over_24h_no_doer') = 0;

-- 3. The failure mode and its detector.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO failure_modes (fm_key, failure_mode, root_cause, remediation, detector, probe_class, first_seen, issue_id, trigger_condition, symptom, blast_radius)
VALUES ('il-duplicate-meaning',
  'IMPROVEMENT-LOOP-1 files a second ticket (METRIC-REGRESSION-1 or METRIC-FIX-RELAPSED-1) for a metric whose trigger an owner directive disabled because another metric keeps its meaning, so one fact is counted and ticketed twice and the extra tickets stay open for as long as the old window stays off target',
  'improvementEvaluate retires a metric only through the explicit marker [superseded by <metric> in metric_registry.target (IL-SUPERSEDED-1); a disabled trigger alone keeps its checks on purpose. BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1 disabled six triggers without the marker, so 12 tickets stood on 2026-10-26 (the cost trio also reads a one-off burst through a trailing 7-day mean for about two weeks)',
  'a migration that disables a trigger as a duplicate appends the marker with its successor to the metric''s registry target in the same file (IL-ONE-MEANING-1); the drill probe of control improvement-loop-superseded-marker checks that the chain ends in a metric with an enabled trigger',
  'fm-il-duplicate-meaning: no open METRIC-REGRESSION-1 or METRIC-FIX-RELAPSED-1 ticket stands on a metric whose triggers BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1 disabled and that carries no superseded marker',
  'fm-il-duplicate-meaning', strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now'), 1000422,
  'an open METRIC-REGRESSION-1 or METRIC-FIX-RELAPSED-1 issue whose metric has every trigger disabled with a BREACH-ONE-MEANING-1 note and no [superseded by marker in metric_registry.target',
  'two to four tickets per metric (regression and relapse) that no loop can act on because the meaning is carried by another ticket, counted in issues_open_over_120m, issues_without_next_action and metric_regressions_7d',
  'the open-issue SLA metrics, the chaos drill of the superseded marker control and the owner''s one-meaning rule');

